@@ -46,6 +46,26 @@ It throws when `patch` is not a syntactically valid JSON Patch document (for exa
 `from` that doesn't resolve within the document, a `test` whose `value` doesn't match, or a `move`
 whose `from` is a proper prefix of its `path`.
 
+`createPatch(from, to)` computes a [JSON Patch](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6902) that turns
+`from` into `to` when applied, describing only what changed between them. It never mutates `from`,
+`to`, or any value reachable from either.
+
+```ts
+import { createPatch, applyPatch } from 'json-toolkit';
+
+const from = { foo: 'bar', baz: 'qux' };
+const to = { foo: 'bar', baz: 'changed' };
+
+createPatch(from, to);
+// => [{ op: 'replace', path: '/baz', value: 'changed' }]
+
+applyPatch(from, createPatch(from, to));
+// => to
+```
+
+Object members are compared by key and array elements by index; a value that only moved position
+(within an object or an array) is reported as an add/remove or replace rather than as a `move`.
+
 ### JSON Merge Patch (RFC 7386)
 
 `applyMergePatch(target, patch)` applies a [JSON Merge Patch](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7386) —
